jobs.description:
For our client in Amsterdam, we are looking for a key account manager (B2B retail) for the German market. Together with your colleagues from the sales team, you will continue to sell a large assortment of cool, practical, and sustainable products. In this position, you are responsible for expanding the customer base and maintaining the current relationships. Your base location will be our NL office; they prefer that you visit your customers in Germany as much as possible to strengthen the relationship and introduce the newest items. The ratio of new client acquisition to existing client management is 50/50.
Responsibilities: - Develop and maintain strong relationships with key accounts in Germany;
- Identify new business opportunities and drive sales growth;
- Negotiate contracts and agreements with clients;
- Provide excellent customer service and support.
- Collaborate with internal teams to meet customer needs;
- Prepare and deliver sales presentations to potential clients;
- Monitor market trends and competitor activities;
- Meet sales targets and objectives;
- Travel within Germany for client meetings and business development.

RequirementsYou know how to find commercial opportunities, and with your strong drive plus a good dose of perseverance and guts, you grab them. Besides:- Commercially driven;
- Positive, enthusiastic, and friendly;
- Experience in sales or account management for a minimum of 7 years and having worked with key accounts for several years; 
- Business fluent in German (C2 level) and English;
- Familiarity with the German retail / FMCG market and consumer trends is a MUST;
- excellent verbal and written communication abilities;
- Strong problem-solving skills and a proven track record of building and maintaining client relationships
- Living near the Amsterdam area (or have plans to relocate there very soon)

Benefits- 13th month bonus
- 8% holiday allowance
- A full-time (40 hour) contract; first contract is for 7 months.
- Fully onsite

Are you accurate and do you enjoy working with different materials and machines? For our client in Waalwijk, we are looking for a Production Employee for the Preparation Department. Together with a team of four colleagues, you will transform bulk materials into precisely sized components used in the production of custom-made sandwich panels.

What will you do?

You will work with materials such as foam, wood, and composite. Using production lists, you will cut and calibrate these materials to the required dimensions.

- Adjust materials to the correct thickness using various saws and calibration machines;
- Cut materials to size at your own workstation;
- Calibrate material thickness using a thickness planer;
- Label components according to the production list and sort them onto transport carts;
- Keep your work area clean and organized.

Since every sandwich panel is custom-made, you will work with different production lists and dimensions every day.

What do we expect from you?

- You work accurately and enjoy working as part of a team;
- You can read production lists or are willing to learn;
- You speak Dutch or English.
